  "id": "Compound::DB01148 - Gene::1128",
  "verbalization": "Flavoxate is linked to Chrm1 through a series of molecular and functional relationships that collectively suggest a role in modulating cholinergic signaling. The evidence indicates that Flavoxate, as part of the Cholinergic Muscarinic Antagonists class, binds to Chrm2, which is a G-protein coupled acetylcholine receptor. This receptor activity is then associated with Chrm1, implying a potential regulatory pathway involving cholinergic receptors. Additionally, Flavoxate is also linked to Solifenacin, another muscarinic antagonist, which similarly binds to Chrm1, reinforcing the involvement of muscarinic receptors in the interaction. The shared classification as an organonitrogen heterocyclic compound and antimuscarinic agent further supports the notion of a common mechanism in modulating cholinergic signaling pathways. The integration of these relationships highlights a potential role for Flavoxate in influencing Chrm1 through muscarinic receptor activation, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
